MGAVIDEO driver init (FUN_0000_0009 + the 0x2 jmp thunk): thread the template-copy / workspace-alloc /
method-vector-reloc cascade.

The video driver's init runs entirely through DGROUP indirect method vectors whose __allregs C bodies
dropped ALL register args.  The init (asm, MGAVIDEO image 0x9..0x91) does, in order:
  5x  f98b(count, srcseg, slot, srcoff)   via [DGROUP:0x36]  -- copy a template from module data into a
                                          freshly allocated DGROUP buffer (patch 034 reconstructs f98b);
  alloc 0x46a paras -> DGROUP:0x3e4       via [DGROUP:0xd4] = FUN_1000_1917  (driver workspace);
  alloc 0x300 bytes -> DGROUP:0x782       via [DGROUP:0xcc] = FUN_1000_182a  (scratch buffer);
  reloc apply over [DGROUP:0x70e]         via [DGROUP:0x12] = FUN_0000_f842  (installs the driver method
                                          vectors, incl. DGROUP:0x540 = 0xe8:load_seg = the VGA mode-set).
With no threaded args f98b's rep-movsb wrote to host NULL -> SIGSEGV (the terminal crash).  Thread every
call with the asm-verified immediates.  The five template srcseg immediates (0x46a/0x52c/0x54b/0x54d/0x608)
and the reloc section's leading seg word are MZ reloc sites (module relocs 0x12/0x21/0x30/0x44/0x58 and
0x52c0), relocated to the driver load-seg at LOAD; model that by adding (fist_mga_base>>4) at the f98b call
sites so the engine copies from the correct absolute module segment, and apply the (already-relocated)
method-vector section verbatim via the loader shim fist_apply_reloc_at (native_main.c).  The 0x2-offset
thunk is a `jmp 0x9` -> it now just calls FUN_0000_0009 (no duplicated body).  This is the first driver-unit
patch (targets the fist_mga.c assemble output).  Asm-verified against MGAVIDEO.DVR base-0 module offsets.
--- a/fist_mga.c
+++ b/fist_mga.c
@@ -763,17 +763,8 @@
